00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:49.910
Alrighty.

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:54.880
Two more things you got to
know before we get to the demo.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:58.010
Trust me, it's only two.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:02.580
So BQ ML is one of the
really big launches

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:05.130
that we've had
here for BigQuery--

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:07.050
it was highlighted in
the keynote earlier--

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:09.420
but this fundamentally
is the ability

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:12.540
to create models, evaluate
models, and predict

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.590
on models all within SQL--

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:16.740
so we've invented
some new SQL verbs,

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:18.480
and all inside the BigQuery UI.

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:22.800
So gone are the days or
needing to export data to GCS,

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:28.590
ingest it in TensorFlow or
Cloud ML Engine or into Spark ML

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:29.160
or whatever.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:31.020
You can do it all
inside at BigQuery.

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:33.150
So that simplifies life a lot.

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:34.994
We're going to use
that in just a second.

00:09:34.994 --> 00:09:36.660
The other thing you
need-- so that's one

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.634
of the basic building blocks.

00:09:38.634 --> 00:09:40.050
The other piece
of information you

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:42.330
need to have before
we get to the demo

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:45.570
is, who's consuming this,
and what's the problem?

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:50.520
So Smart Cities is a
data-driven initiative

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.490
to try to alleviate some of
the traffic or infrastructure

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:56.730
congestion problems that
are plaguing cities,

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:59.010
not just in the states,
but around the world.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:01.980
And so growth-- and this is
a really significant thing.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:05.280
This is not just us spending
more time in traffic

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:08.340
as we go to and from work.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:11.100
Decreases in the ability of
folks to move around cities

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:14.160
is materially impacting
accessibility to jobs,

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:15.990
accessibility to opportunity.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:17.910
It creates incredibly
high gradients

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:20.640
in housing prices, which makes
markets a little bit less

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.020
stable.

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:26.370
And it speaks also to
environmental sustainability

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:28.810
and the quality of life
that we have in our cities.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:30.340
So it's a big problem.

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:32.710
And by applying data
and analytics to it,

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:35.820
we might be able to use our
infrastructure much more

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:37.000
efficiently.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.499
Now, the cynical among us, or
at least the data cynical--

00:10:39.499 --> 00:10:41.040
and I imagine there
are very few data

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:45.930
cynics in this particular
audience given the crew here,

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:49.960
but the data cynics might
ask, well, you know what?

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:51.450
Why don't we just build more?

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.870
Well, Seattle--
that's where I live--

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:58.200
can not handle a
400 lane highway.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:10:59.730
There's just not enough room.

00:10:59.730 --> 00:11:01.500
So we have to use
data and analytics

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:04.320
to do things like optimizing--

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:06.360
like real-time
adaptive spotlights

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:09.150
on streets,
ride-shares that data

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:11.730
and analytics heavy application.

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:16.440
My favorite one on this list,
ride-share and flying cars.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:17.010
All right.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:19.110
So all of these
techniques are heavily

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:23.670
reliant on data and
analytics, and so we have

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:25.260
to produce these technologies.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.550
Google has to produce
these features

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:29.190
so that companies
like Geotab can

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:33.150
help smart cities decide how to
use their infrastructure more

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:34.710
wisely--

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:38.090
and so we've covered
a couple of things.

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:40.000
We've covered the launch, right?

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:42.140
So BQ ML, BQ GIS.

00:11:42.140 --> 00:11:44.600
We covered the viz tools,
we covered the background

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:47.240
information-- and with that,
I will give up the stage

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:48.760
and let the main act come on on.

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:49.959
Bob?

00:11:49.959 --> 00:11:51.042
